  ok   a YES buyer at 95c on a YES market: kept, won
  ok   a NO buyer at 95c on a YES market: kept, LOST -- the grid needs losers
  ok   NULL: 10c is kept by nobody
  ok   a 75c buy is scanned (the reversal screen needs it) but sits in no GRID cell
  ok   NULL: 200 s is beyond the window
  ok   NULL: no settlement on file -> skipped, not guessed
  ok   bands place 20 s in 16-30 and 96c in 95-98; 99.5c falls outside every price band
  ok   a boundary value belongs to ONE band: 95c to 95-98, 90c to 90-95, 99c to the closed last band, 5 s to 0-5, 6 s to 6-15
  ok   grid: 3 trades, 1 lost, 50 contracts of which 10 lost
  ok   cell EV = (1-q)(1-p) - q p - fee, at the cell's own mean price
  ok   NULL: an empty cell has no EV
  ok   one market, one flip
  ok   the new-side buyer at 75c with 20 s left is recorded as RIGHT
  ok   ...and the 92c buyer at 5 s in the 90c+ bucket
  ok   NULL: the favourite WON -> no flip, no rows, and its late rows are NOT kept in memory
  ok   a market with no favourite at 60 s keeps NO late rows -- most markets are like this
  ok   the wobble is the LOWEST price the favourite's side implied inside the window, from either side's trades: a NO buyer paying 45c puts the YES favourite at 55c
  ok   wobble to 50-70c: 1 market, favourite lost; stayed at 90c+: 1 market, favourite won -- conditioned on the price, not the outcome
  ok   the cache round-trip preserves the grid, the favourites and the wobbles
pingrid selftest: OK
